          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ba17fd668ccc825e7ea36fea5b71b7a24819f6fd",
          "message": "AArch64: Add native compress, decompress and frombytes\n\nThe AArch64 backend left nine slots of mlkem/src/native/api.h to the C\nfallback: poly_compress_d{4,5,10,11}, poly_decompress_d{4,5,10,11} and\npoly_frombytes. Add Neon kernels for all of them, with HOL-Light proofs\nof functional correctness and of constant-time and memory safety, CBMC\nproofs of the meta.h wrappers, and the accepted HOLTrace files.\n\nDecode: for d = 5 and 10, TBL gathers the two bytes of each coefficient\ninto a 16-bit lane, USHL by per-lane amounts and AND isolate it at bit\n12 - d, and one SQRDMULH by 3329 << 3 yields Decompress_d. For d = 11,\ntwo of every 8 coefficients span three bytes; a second TBL and SLI\nfetch them, and they end up at other bits, so mask and multiplier\ndiffer per lane. For d = 4, TBL looks up the low and high result byte\nin two 16-entry tables, with no multiply. frombytes needs no TBL: LD3\nsplits 3-byte groups, and AND, ZIP1/ZIP2 and USHR form the\ncoefficients.\n\nEncode: SQRDMULH by round(2^(w-1+d) / 3329) on w-bit lanes gives y\nwith y mod 2^d = Compress_d(u); the SLI of the packing does the\nreduction. d = 5 works on 16-bit lanes. d = 10 and 11 need 32-bit\nlanes and are straight-line code that writes each 10- or 11-byte group\nwith a 16-byte ST1, overwritten in part by the next. For d = 4, no\n16-bit constant is exact: SQDMULH by 2520, then (x + 8) >> 4 on bytes,\nand SRI packs two nibbles per byte.\n\nThe decompress kernels and compress_d5 load their constants from a\ntable that the caller passes, generated by autogen for C and HOL-Light.\nByte buffers use byte-lane structure loads and stores only, so they\nmay have any alignment. SLOTHY does not optimize these kernels yet:\ndev/aarch64_opt/src/Makefile copies them unchanged, as for rej_uniform.\ndev/aarch64_clean/README.md describes each approach.\n\nCycles per call on Neoverse V1, C fallback in parentheses:\n\n              d4        d5        d10        d11\n  decompress  50 (72)   65 (405)  68 (456)   95 (466)\n  compress    43 (122)  77 (353)  110 (384)  150 (522)\n  frombytes   57 (77)\n\nSigned-off-by: Hanno Becker <beckphan@amazon.co.uk>",
